I love the new dragon scale mails and love having the option of more
than a redundant resistance but "GDSM and SDSM are far from the
best" ?  I disagree ...
Green - passive poison attack --- very fun but not as good/protective
as reflection or MR, so would you wish for it?;
Red - +d6 damage to all attacks --- meh, but I haven't tried it so...
Blue - The player gains the "very fast" intrinsic --- this is good,
allows for very fast _and_ jumping boots without needing haste, but
again not as good/protective as reflection or MR so would you wish for
it if you didn't already have reflection and MR?;
Yellow - confusion and stunning resistance --- it's wise to keep the
scales in one's inventory but there is only one case where confusion/
stunning is game-threatening and taking off one's cloak and armor to
portal search in the planes seems rather brazen;
Orange - passive sleep attack  --- very fun but not as good/protective
as reflection or MR, so would you wish for it?;
Black - passive blindness attack --- cute but not as good/protective
as reflection or MR, so would you wish for it?;
White - variant of "water walking" --- but then how do I dip my
potions?  I don't know if this works for the Plane of Water, but if it
doesn't I might as well just levitate.

One still needs MR and reflection and with a limited number of wishes,
and enchant armor scrolls, it'd be unwise IMO to wish for things that
you don't need, or enchant a spare set of armor.

Oh, and I almost forgot about Gold Dragon Scale Mail ... too bad the
radius isn't the same as a lamp, otherwise I'd probably wear it.
Also, I'm still shy about my gold dragon riding accident and haven't
wanted to experience any further trickeries (if they exist).

